    "slot_value": "A documented exception is allowed only when the issue is low impact, tightly bounded to a specific record or small batch, and there is no material risk of wrong routing or service disruption if proceeding; it also needs a clear compensating control, such as a planned correction window, so it is not left open-ended. If the business owner is unavailable or declines to accept the risk, approval should fall to a delegated operations manager or duty executive with the same authority level; if no one at that level is reachable, the item remains blocked, and frontline staff should not make the call on their own. For portability synchronization issues, keep the issue open for provider action when the fix requires the originating provider to correct source data or confirm a disputed status; use a temporary workaround or manual reconciliation only when the issue is limited, reversible, and an audit trail can be preserved without changing the underlying business truth. If a workaround would mask the real problem or create a second inconsistency later, do not use it and leave the issue open until the provider responds.",
