    "slot_key": "Portability record contents",
    "slot_value": "A portability record is the authoritative data entry kept for each number or transaction so all participants can see its current status, ownership history, and routing state; it is used to keep everyone synchronized and to support audit and reporting later. During migration, old data must be mapped carefully into the new system so transaction history and current routing status are preserved. It must also preserve the original request data and any resolution notes so the disruption can be reconciled later and reported on. Staff should see the transaction identifiers, the provider names involved, the timestamps, the current status, the decision trail, and any validation or exception notes tied to the case. They also need enough subscriber reference data to match the case correctly, but not necessarily the full customer profile.",
    "operation": "refine"
